# Chroma library, modern Earth: title moments of three green everyday entry jobs (v22.4). Library thread, 2026-10-10,
# from Packs' chroma-packs/notes/v22.4-green-entries-for-library.md: green-led lives had no first job of their own.
# An everyday pair per title that only its holder meets (holds:), in the style of earth-spheres-first-jobs.lib: the
# first moment is the job's everyday trouble, the second a turning point in it (Packs' "step").
# Syntax: header of build.py. Rules: SPEC.md. Every moment carries sphere: <sphere>, every option the face it acts in
# (a cross option X>Y the means colour's face). ladder: is the rung the job sits on in that face's ladder.
# Evenness: every one-colour option has chance 75 and every cross option 65, so each colour's mean is the same.
# Pairs (complementary calls):
#   gardener or groundskeeper  GU (s3) / WBR (s4)     farm hand  GR (s1) / WUB (s2)     animal care worker  GW (s3) / UBR (s4)
# Juvenile holders (farm hand from 14, the others from 16) meet nothing about drink or bars here.

# ================================================================ gardener or groundskeeper (prod.G)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls GU (cycle s3); partner: the parks contract goes to a cheaper firm

== the old oak by the playing field
tier: everyday
sphere: prod
ladder: known
at: employer
rate: 0.5
share: .01
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-75
calls: GU
holds: gardener or groundskeeper
tone: mixed
life: work, nature
horizon: weeks
roles: boss, colleague
earth: after a storm the school wants the old oak by the playing field felled, and you think it can be saved
times: Most groundskeepers at a school or a park, once or twice in their years there; storm damage to old trees is a common grounds problem (estimate)
gap: 1-3
scene: A branch came down from the old oak by the playing field in last week's storm, and {boss} wants the whole tree felled before term starts. {N} has looked after that oak for years and thinks careful pruning would make it safe. The tree crew is booked for Friday.
scene W: The children's safety comes first, and the decision is not {Ns} to make. {N} still owes {boss} an honest view.
scene U: {N} has checked the wood: the branch that fell was dead, and the rest of the tree is sound.
scene B: {boss} signs off {Ns} contract renewal next month.
scene R: {N} loves that tree, and the thought of the saw going in on Friday makes {N} angry.
scene G: The oak was old when the school was built. Generations of children have sat in its shade.
- W | put the risk in writing, and leave the decision to the head | v: conformity, security | sphere: prod.W | chance: 75
- U | walk the head round the tree, and show which wood is dead and which is sound | v: universalism, achievement | sphere: prod.U | chance: 75
- B | agree to the felling, and ask to keep the timber to sell | v: power, achievement | sphere: prod.B | chance: 75
- R | tell the head straight that felling it would be a shame they will all regret | v: self-direction, stimulation | sphere: prod.R | chance: 75
- G | prune it carefully yourself over the weekend, the way the old gardeners did | act: prune it carefully themselves over the weekend, the way the old gardeners did | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: prod.G | chance: 75
- W>R | fence off the tree today, and push hard for a second opinion before Friday | v: security, self-direction | sphere: prod.W | chance: 65
- U>G | get a tree surgeon to check it, and plant a young oak beside it anyway | v: universalism, tradition | sphere: prod.U | chance: 65
- B>W | let the felling go ahead, and make sure the paperwork says it was not your call | act: let the felling go ahead, and make sure the paperwork says it was not their call | v: security, conformity | sphere: prod.B | chance: 65
- R>U | take off every dead limb yourself before Friday, safely roped in | act: take off every dead limb themselves before Friday, safely roped in | v: stimulation, achievement | sphere: prod.R | chance: 65
- G>B | ask the parents who sat under it as children to speak to the head | v: tradition, power | sphere: prod.G | chance: 65
works: {boss} takes {Ns} view seriously, and the playing field is safe again by the start of term.
works: Parents stop {N} at the gate to say they were glad someone cared about the old tree.
fails: {boss} takes it as {N} overstepping, and the contract comes back with fewer hours.
fails: The week turns into one long argument with the tree crew, and {N} comes out of it worn thin.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls WBR (cycle s4); partner: the old oak by the playing field

== the parks contract goes to a cheaper firm
tier: everyday
sphere: prod
ladder: known
at: employer
rate: 0.5
share: .008
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-75
calls: WBR
holds: gardener or groundskeeper
tone: trouble
life: work, money
horizon: months
roles: boss, colleague
earth: the parks contract goes to a cheaper firm, which will keep you on for less pay and wants the beds sprayed
times: Most grounds workers on council or contract work meet a change of contractor at least once; such contracts are often let again every few years (estimate)
gap: 2-5
scene: The council has given the parks contract to a cheaper firm. {N} can stay on under the new firm, on less pay and with orders to spray the beds instead of weeding them by hand. The new manager wants an answer by Monday.
scene W: {N} took the job to keep the parks safe and tidy for everyone, whoever holds the contract.
scene U: {N} knows what the spray will do to the beds and the pond within a year.
scene B: Less pay is still pay, and the new firm will need someone who knows every bed.
scene R: {N} feels like walking off the job today and leaving them to it.
scene G: {N} has worked these parks for years, alongside people who are not being kept on.
- W | stay on and keep the parks up to standard, whatever the new firm pays | v: conformity, benevolence | sphere: prod.W | chance: 75
- U | write the new manager a plan showing hand weeding costs less over a year | v: achievement, universalism | sphere: prod.U | chance: 75
- B | stay on, but only as head of the crew, with a raise to match | v: power, achievement | sphere: prod.B | chance: 75
- R | turn the job down on the spot, and look for work somewhere that cares | v: self-direction, stimulation | sphere: prod.R | chance: 75
- G | stay on with the old crew, and keep weeding by hand where you can | act: stay on with the old crew, and keep weeding by hand where they can | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: prod.G | chance: 75
- W>G | stay on, and ask the council to keep the old beds off the spray list | v: conformity, tradition | sphere: prod.W | chance: 65
- U>W | take the facts about the spray to the council's next open meeting | v: universalism, conformity | sphere: prod.U | chance: 65
- B>U | take the job, learn the new firm's books, and bid for the contract yourself next time | act: take the job, learn the new firm's books, and bid for the contract themselves next time | v: power, achievement | sphere: prod.B | chance: 65
- R>B | tell the new manager you will stay only if the spraying stops, and mean it | act: tell the new manager they will stay only if the spraying stops, and mean it | v: self-direction, power | sphere: prod.R | chance: 65
- G>R | leave with the old crew and start a garden firm of your own together | act: leave with the old crew and start a garden firm of their own together | v: tradition, stimulation | sphere: prod.G | chance: 65
works: Two of the old crew find work again through {N}, and they do not forget it.
works: Whatever {N} chose, by summer the parks still look cared for, and people say so.
fails: The spray goes down anyway, and by autumn the pond has turned a dull, cloudy brown.
fails: Money is tight for {N} through the winter that follows.

# ================================================================ farm hand (prod.G)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls GR (cycle s1); partner: asked to stay on for the winter

== a storm coming and the hay still down
tier: everyday
sphere: prod
ladder: known
at: employer
rate: 0.5
share: .01
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 14-70
calls: GR
holds: farm hand
tone: trouble
life: work, nature
horizon: moment
roles: boss, neighbour
earth: a storm is coming tonight, half the hay is still lying in the field, and the farmer cannot be reached
times: Most farm hands, a few times a season; weather racing the harvest is the commonest pressure of farm work (estimate)
gap: 0.5-1
scene: The forecast says a storm will break tonight, and half the hay is still lying in the low field. {boss} has gone to market and is not answering the phone. {N} has the keys to the tractor and two hours of light left.
scene W: {boss} left clear orders for today, and bringing in hay was not on the list.
scene U: {N} looks at the sky and the field, and works out how much can be baled before dark.
scene B: If {N} saves the hay, {boss} owes {N}, and {boss} is not one to forget a debt.
scene R: {N} wants to be on that tractor right now, racing the storm.
scene G: {N} has watched the old hands on this farm read the sky for years. They would already be moving.
- W | keep to the day's orders, and keep trying the farmer's phone | v: conformity, security | sphere: prod.W | chance: 75
- U | bale the driest rows first, and cover the rest with sheets from the barn | v: achievement, security | sphere: prod.U | chance: 75
- B | ring the farm next door, and offer them a share of the hay for a hand | v: power, achievement | sphere: prod.B | chance: 75
- R | get on the tractor and bring in as much as you can before the rain | act: get on the tractor and bring in as much as they can before the rain | v: stimulation, self-direction | sphere: prod.R | chance: 75
- G | pile it into haycocks on the high ground, the way the old hands did | v: tradition | sphere: prod.G | chance: 75
- W>U | finish the day's list, then send the farmer a clear plan to say yes to | v: conformity, achievement | sphere: prod.W | chance: 65
- U>B | save what you can, and make sure the farmer knows exactly what it was worth | act: save what they can, and make sure the farmer knows exactly what it was worth | v: achievement, power | sphere: prod.U | chance: 65
- B>R | leave the hay: it is not your farm, and you are not paid for storms | act: leave the hay: it is not their farm, and they are not paid for storms | v: hedonism, self-direction | sphere: prod.B | chance: 65
- R>G | wake the whole family at the farm and get everyone out to the field | v: stimulation, benevolence | sphere: prod.R | chance: 65
- G>W | gather the neighbours, as farms round here always have, and bring it in together | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: prod.G | chance: 65
works: {boss} hears how {N} handled the storm and says little, but the next week's pay is more than it should be.
works: By morning the storm has passed, and {boss} and {N} walk the wet field together.
fails: The storm comes early, and most of the hay is lost in the field.
fails: {boss} is angry about how {N} handled it, whatever was saved.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls WUB (cycle s2); partner: a storm coming and the hay still down

== asked to stay on for the winter
tier: everyday
sphere: prod
ladder: known
at: employer
rate: 0.5
share: .008
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-70
calls: WUB
holds: farm hand
tone: mixed
life: work, home
horizon: months
roles: boss
earth: the harvest is in, and the farmer asks you to stay on through the winter for half the summer's pay
times: Many farm hands, at the end of each season; much farm work is seasonal, and only some hands are kept on through the winter (estimate)
gap: 1-3
scene: The harvest is in, and {boss} asks {N} to stay on through the winter: feeding the stock in the dark mornings and mending fences, for half the summer's pay. In town there is steadier work with a roof over it.
scene W: {boss} kept every promise through the summer. {N} feels bound to do the same.
scene U: {N} sets a winter on the farm against a year of training somewhere warm, and does the sums.
scene B: {boss} has no children who want the place. Staying on could lead somewhere.
scene R: The dark mornings sound grim. Town has friends, noise and nights out.
scene G: The stock know {N} now. The fields feel more like home than anywhere else.
- W | stay the winter, as you would want someone to do for you | act: stay the winter, as they would want someone to do for them | v: benevolence, conformity | sphere: prod.W | chance: 75
- U | stay, and use the dark evenings to study for a farming certificate | v: achievement, self-direction | sphere: prod.U | chance: 75
- B | stay on, if the farmer puts in writing a share of the spring lambs | v: power, security | sphere: prod.B | chance: 75
- R | take the steadier work in town, and come back for the harvest if you miss it | act: take the steadier work in town, and come back for the harvest if they miss it | v: stimulation, hedonism | sphere: prod.R | chance: 75
- G | stay without a second thought: the stock need feeding, and you belong here | act: stay without a second thought: the stock need feeding, and they belong here | v: tradition, security | sphere: prod.G | chance: 75
- W>B | stay the winter, and ask fairly for a proper wage from spring | v: conformity, power | sphere: prod.W | chance: 65
- U>R | stay, and talk the farmer into trying a new crop on the bottom field | v: self-direction, stimulation | sphere: prod.U | chance: 65
- B>G | stay, and quietly save every coin toward a few acres of your own | act: stay, and quietly save every coin toward a few acres of their own | v: security, tradition | sphere: prod.B | chance: 65
- R>W | go to town for the winter, but promise to be back for lambing, and keep it | v: stimulation, conformity | sphere: prod.R | chance: 65
- G>U | stay, and ask the farmer to teach you everything about the land | act: stay, and ask the farmer to teach them everything about the land | v: tradition, achievement | sphere: prod.G | chance: 65
works: The choice sits well with {N}, and {boss} shakes {Ns} hand on it.
works: Whatever the winter brings, {N} comes out of it surer of what {N} wants.
fails: The winter is long and lonely, and {N} spends much of it wishing for the other road.
fails: {boss} runs short of money in the new year, and what was promised comes late.

# ================================================================ animal care worker (care.G)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls GW (cycle s3); partner: the vet asks you to come and assist

== a frightened dog at closing time
tier: everyday
sphere: care
ladder: known
at: employer
rate: 0.5
share: .007
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-70
calls: GW
holds: animal care worker
tone: trouble
life: work, community
horizon: moment
roles: boss, colleague
earth: the shelter is full, and at closing time someone brings in a frightened dog they found by the road
times: Most shelter workers, often; shelters in many places run full for much of the year (estimate)
gap: 0.5-1
scene: The shelter is full, and {boss} has said no more intakes this week. At closing time a woman comes to the door holding a thin, frightened dog she found by the road. {N} is the only one still on shift.
scene W: The rule on intakes is there for a reason: too many animals, and all of them suffer.
scene U: {N} knows which kennels might free up tomorrow, and what the dog is likely to need tonight.
scene B: Breaking {Ns} manager's rule could cost {N} a place on the next rota, or worse.
scene R: The dog is shaking. {N} cannot bear to shut the door on it.
scene G: The old hands at the shelter used to say no animal is turned away at night.
- W | explain the rule kindly, and give her the number of the shelter in the next town | v: conformity, benevolence | sphere: care.W | chance: 75
- U | check the dog over, then find the one kennel that can be shared tonight | v: achievement, benevolence | sphere: care.U | chance: 75
- B | take the dog in, and log it as arriving tomorrow morning | v: security, power | sphere: care.B | chance: 75
- R | take the dog home with you tonight, whatever anyone says | act: take the dog home with them tonight, whatever anyone says | v: benevolence, self-direction | sphere: care.R | chance: 75
- G | take it in, as the old hands always did, and face the manager tomorrow | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: care.G | chance: 75
- W>R | ring the manager at home now, and ask plainly for one exception | v: conformity, self-direction | sphere: care.W | chance: 65
- U>G | ask the woman to foster the dog overnight, and show her how to settle it | v: universalism, benevolence | sphere: care.U | chance: 65
- B>W | turn her away by the rules, and make sure the log says you did | act: turn her away by the rules, and make sure the log says they did | v: security, conformity | sphere: care.B | chance: 65
- R>U | take the dog in tonight, then spend tomorrow finding it a home | v: stimulation, achievement | sphere: care.R | chance: 65
- G>B | call round the old volunteers until one of them takes the dog for the night | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: care.G | chance: 65
works: Within a fortnight the dog has a home, and the woman writes to thank the shelter.
works: The woman comes back a week later with a donation and a friend who wants to volunteer.
fails: {boss} hears about it and gives {N} a formal warning.
fails: The night goes badly, and {N} goes home certain they got it wrong.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- everyday, calls UBR (cycle s4); partner: a frightened dog at closing time

== the vet asks you to come and assist
tier: everyday
sphere: care
ladder: known
at: employer
rate: 0.5
share: .005
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-70
calls: UBR
holds: animal care worker
tone: mixed
life: work, money
horizon: years
roles: boss, colleague
earth: the vet who visits the shelter asks you to come and work at the practice as an assistant
times: Some animal care workers, once in their years at a shelter; vets' practices often take their assistants from the kennels and shelters they visit (estimate)
gap: 2-6
scene: The vet who comes to the shelter on Thursdays asks {N} to work at the practice as an assistant: better pay and proper training, but it means leaving the shelter, which is already short-staffed. The vet wants an answer by the end of the month.
scene W: The shelter needs {N}. So will the animals that come through the practice.
scene U: The training would teach {N} things the shelter never could.
scene B: Better pay, a proper post, and a vet who could write {N} a reference for anything.
scene R: {N} loves the bustle of the shelter, and the thought of a quiet surgery feels tame.
scene G: {N} thinks of the shelter's regulars, the old dogs and the volunteers, and what leaving would mean to them.
- W | take the post, but stay on at the shelter one weekend a month | v: benevolence, conformity | sphere: care.W | chance: 75
- U | take the post for the training, and plan to qualify further | v: achievement, self-direction | sphere: care.U | chance: 75
- B | use the offer to ask the shelter for a raise, and see who pays more | v: power, achievement | sphere: care.B | chance: 75
- R | say no: the shelter is where your heart is | act: say no: the shelter is where their heart is | v: self-direction, benevolence | sphere: care.R | chance: 75
- G | stay at the shelter, with the people and the animals you know | act: stay at the shelter, with the people and the animals they know | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: care.G | chance: 75
- W>G | stay at the shelter, and ask the vet to train the volunteers instead | v: benevolence, tradition | sphere: care.W | chance: 65
- U>W | take the post, and write the shelter a handbook before you go | act: take the post, and write the shelter a handbook before they go | v: achievement, benevolence | sphere: care.U | chance: 65
- B>U | take the post, and learn enough to run a practice of your own one day | act: take the post, and learn enough to run a practice of their own one day | v: achievement, power | sphere: care.B | chance: 65
- R>B | take the post today, and tell the shelter's manager it was long overdue | v: stimulation, power | sphere: care.R | chance: 65
- G>R | stay, and talk the vet into a free clinic at the shelter on Saturdays | v: tradition, stimulation | sphere: care.G | chance: 65
works: Whatever {N} chose, it sits right, and the animals in {Ns} care are better for it.
works: The vet keeps in touch, and passes on whatever {N} needs to know.
fails: Within a month {N} is second-guessing the choice, and lies awake over it.
fails: Word of the offer gets round the shelter, and some of the volunteers are cool with {N} for a while.
